<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">British Museum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The British Museum is a public museum in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a> founded in 1753, holding one of the world's largest collections of human history and culture. It houses Assyrian palace reliefs, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lion-hunt-of-ashurbanipal">lion hunt reliefs</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashurbanipal">Ashurbanipal</a> from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nineveh">Nineveh</a>. It also holds a large collection of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/benin-bronzes">Benin Bronzes</a> taken in 1897, which are at the centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/repatriation-of-cultural-property">restitution</a> debates.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/british-museum.jpg" alt="British Museum" width="320" height="230" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ham · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:British_Museum_from_NE_2.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
